+# noc_balance (Perf round 1, BH p100a). NoC0 reads have a y-gradient under all-core load (top rows slowest)
+# and NoC1 carries every write. While most cores own one row, the heavy (larger-share) cores read on NoC1
+# and the bottom half of the grid writes on NoC0. Not applied when most cores own >= 2 rows: writes of
+# row k then overlap NoC0 reads of row k+1 (measured +10% with the writer half alone).
+NOC_BALANCE = True

